.TH ICY 7 "May 2026" "ICY" "Miscellaneous Information"
.SH NAME
ICY \- in\-band metadata format used by Shoutcast and Icecast streams
.SH DESCRIPTION
ICY metadata is an in\-band metadata protocol originally introduced by
Shoutcast for MP3 internet radio streams. It is also supported by Icecast
for MP3 and AAC (ADTS) streams. ICY metadata is inserted into the audio
byte stream at fixed intervals defined by the
.B icy\-metaint
header.
.PP
The server sends HTTP\-style headers such as:
.PP
.nf
icy\-metaint: N
icy\-name: Station Name
icy\-genre: Genre
icy\-url: Station URL
.fi
.PP
The value of
.B icy\-metaint
specifies the number of audio bytes between metadata blocks. After exactly
N bytes of audio, the server inserts a metadata block consisting of:
.PP
.RS
1 byte: length indicator (L), where metadata length is L * 16 bytes  
.br
L*16 bytes: metadata payload (may be zero\-length)
.RE
.PP
The metadata payload is a semicolon\-separated list of key/value pairs,
typically including:
.PP
.nf
StreamTitle='Artist \- Track';
StreamUrl='https://example.com/';
.fi
.PP
If L is zero, no metadata is present and playback continues immediately
with the next audio byte.
.PP
ICY metadata is not aligned to codec frame boundaries. Clients must count
raw audio bytes and detect metadata blocks even when they fall inside
.BR read (2)
calls. The
.B icy\-metaint
value may be any positive integer and is not required to be even or
aligned.
.PP
ICY metadata is supported only by continuous audio streams such as MP3 and
AAC (ADTS). Segmented streaming formats such as HLS and DASH do not
support ICY metadata.
.SH IMPLEMENTATION NOTES
A correct ICY client must:
.PP
.RS
\&\bullet\ count audio bytes until icy\-metaint is reached  
.br
\&\bullet\ handle partial and oversized reads  
.br
\&\bullet\ handle metadata blocks of length zero  
.br
\&\bullet\ strip metadata bytes before passing audio to a decoder  
.br
\&\bullet\ tolerate odd or changing icy\-metaint values  
.br
\&\bullet\ avoid assuming alignment to codec frames  
.RE
.PP
Failure to handle these conditions may result in corrupted audio, decoder
errors, or loss of metadata.
.SH EXAMPLES
A typical metadata block:
.PP
.nf
StreamTitle='Example Artist \- Example Track';
StreamUrl='https://example.com/';
.fi
.PP
A zero\-length metadata block:
.PP
.nf
(length byte = 0)
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
icyext(1), ffmpeg(1), shoutcast(7), icecast(7)
.SH HISTORY
The ICY protocol originated with Shoutcast in the late 1990s and was later
adopted by Icecast for compatibility.
